ravi: quick heads-up — HF chat_template with nested macros is dropping the system role during hf->redwood conversion. repro below.

ravi:
```jinja
{% macro part(role, text) -%}
{{ role }}: {{ text }}
{%- endmacro %}

{% call part('system', system_msg) %}
{{ system_msg }}
{% endcall %}

{% call part('user', user_msg) %}
{{ user_msg }}
{% endcall %}
```

elaine: can you paste the converted prompt output?

ravi:
```text
user: Hi
user: Hello, can you summarize?
```

tj: possible cause: jinja's whitespace-trimming + empty system_msg means the macro call becomes a no-op and our converter doesn't see the role marker. If system_msg == "" the role line is lost.

ravi: confirmed — config.json for this model sets system_msg = "" for compatibility. two fixes: 1) set a non-empty sentinel (e.g., "<|system|>") 2) update converter to detect macro call patterns and inject explicit role markers when macro exists.

model-onboard-bot: Model onboarding check failed :warning: rendered_roles != expected_roles (system missing)

elaine: short-term patch: during conversion, replace nested-macro calls with explicit markers. e.g. regex: `re.sub(r"{%\s*call part\(\'system\'.*?%}.*?{%\s*endcall\s*%}", "<<SYSTEM>>", s, flags=re.S)`

tj: also watch tokenizer special_tokens in config.json — if sentinel is '', tokenization can collapse boundary. Recommend adding a single-token sentinel like `<|system|>` and add to tokenizer.special_tokens.

ravi: thanks — i'll try the sentinel first and open a PR to add converter detection + unit test.
